---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Quote } from "lucide-react";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Letter from Our Founder | In the Room With Legacy"
  description="A personal letter from the founder of In the Room with Legacy™, sharing the journey and vision behind our mission."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="py-24 md:py-32 bg-primary/5 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0 opacity-5">
      <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,'); background-size: 60px 60px;"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="container relative z-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-display font-bold tracking-tight text-primary leading-tight mb-6">
          Letter from Our Founder
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-foreground/80 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          A personal story of why In the Room with Legacy™ exists
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Letter Content Section -->
  <section class="py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-12">
          <div class="flex justify-center">
            <div class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center">
              <Quote className="text-primary w-12 h-12" />
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
            <p class="lead text-xl text-primary font-medium mb-8">
              Dear Friend,
            </p>
            
            <p>
              I never planned to build a company focused on legacy. Like many important things in life, it found me through personal experience.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              When my grandmother passed away, our family was left with a beautiful home filled with memories, photographs, and artifacts that told the story of our family's journey. But we were also left with questions, confusion, and the weight of having to make decisions without her guidance.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              "Why didn't we have these conversations while she was still here?" I wondered. "Why do so many families wait until crisis or death to talk about what matters most?"
            </p>
            
            <p>
              That experience sparked a journey to understand how families successfully navigate transitions and preserve what matters across generations. I spent years interviewing families, studying wealth transfer, and diving deep into the cultural practices that help communities maintain identity and cohesion across time.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              What I discovered was both troubling and hopeful:
            </p>
            
            <ul>
              <li>Most families are unprepared for major transitions, with up to 70% of wealth transfers failing by the second generation</li>
              <li>Conversations about legacy often happen too late or not at all</li>
              <li>Many families have incredible cultural and social capital that goes unrecognized and uncultivated</li>
              <li>Simple but powerful practices can dramatically improve how families preserve and pass on what matters</li>
            </ul>
            
            <p>
              In the Room with Legacy™ was born from this realization. Our name reflects our core belief that the most important legacy work happens when we're present – in the room – with our loved ones, having the conversations that matter while we still can.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              Today, we're building tools, resources, and experiences that help families of all backgrounds define and preserve their legacies. Whether you're a first-generation builder, an inheritor navigating complex family dynamics, or simply someone who cares about maintaining connection across generations, we're here to meet you where you are.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              Legacy isn't just what you leave behind. It's what you live, share, and protect while you're here.
            </p>
            
            <p>
              I hope you'll join us in the room.
            </p>
            
            <p class="text-lg font-medium text-primary mt-8">
              With gratitude,<br>
              [Founder Name]<br>
              Founder & CEO
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="text-center mt-8">
            <a 
              href="/about" 
              class={buttonVariants({
                variant: "outline",
                class: "border-primary text-primary hover:bg-primary/10 font-medium"
              })}
            >
              Return to About
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>